[38;5;231m⏺[39m Added to [38;5;153mindex.html:12-31[39m:

  - A [38;5;153m.task[39m label wrapping a native [38;5;153m<input type="checkbox">[39m and its text. Wrapping in [38;5;153m<label>[39m makes the text clickable
    too.
  - One CSS rule ([38;5;153minput:checked + span[39m) that strikes through the label when checked, so "done" is visible.

  No JavaScript — the checkbox element holds the on/off state itself. Uncommitted; there are no tests in this repo, and
  I verified only by reading the markup, not by opening it in a browser.

  One thing to flag: I hardcoded a single placeholder item ("Write the thing") since the page had an empty [38;5;153m<main>[39m and no
  item data. If items will come from somewhere (a list, a data source, user input), say the word and I'll wire the
  checkbox into that instead.

